mat="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NHK SPRING CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO ELECTRIC INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAGUCHI SHIGERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MASUDA MICHIYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NATUME YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAGUCHI, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASUDA, MICHIYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NATUME, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical device (1) comprises a substrate (11), an optical waveguide (12), a laser diode (13), a photodiode (14a, 14b), and a filter (15). The substrate (11) includes a smooth reference surface (16) and V-grooves (17) formed in the reference surface (16). Pins (6) are engaged with V-grooves (17) in the device (1) and V-grooves (5) in a connector (2). The optical waveguide (12) is formed on the reference surface (16) and includes a core (21) and a clad (22). The core (21) extends along the reference surface (16). The laser diode (13) emits signal light of a first wavelength toward the core (21) and the photodiode (14a). The filter (15) transmits the signal light of the first wavelength and reflects signal light of second wavelength. The signal light reflected by the filter (15) is received by the photodiode (14b).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un dispositif optique (1) comprend un substrat (11), un guide d'onde optique (12), une diode-laser (13), une photodiode (14a, 14b) et un filtre (15). Le substrat (11) se compose d'une surface de référence lisse (16) dans laquelle des rainures en V (17) sont formées. Des broches (6) sont engagées dans les rainures en V (17) du dispositif, un connecteur (2) étant engagé dans les rainures en V (5). Le guide d'onde optique (12) est formé sur la surface de référence (16) et présente un coeur (21) et une enveloppe (22). Le coeur (21) s'étend le long de la surface de référence (16). La diode-laser (13) émet un signal lumineux à une première longueur d'onde, en direction du coeur (21) et de la photodiode (14a). Le filtre (15) émet le signal lumineux à une première longueur d'onde et réfléchit le signal lumineux à une deuxième longueur d'onde. Le signal lumineux réfléchi par le filtre(15) est reçu par la photodiode (14b).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>